WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.267
Hi, I'm Birch!

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:06.176
Beacon records what your coding agents do, then asks a decision model

00:00:06.176 --> 00:00:08.130
which runs are worth learning from.

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:13.352
Most setups put a decision model inside the loop.

00:00:13.352 --> 00:00:17.521
Beacon puts it after: it grades finished runs offline, and turns the

00:00:17.521 --> 00:00:18.911
promising ones into skills.

00:00:20.425 --> 00:00:25.367
Beacon captures sessions from twenty-nine agent harnesses, through hooks, pollers and a

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:28.250
browser extension, into one typed event stream.

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:32.575
On command, a finished trace, cut to six fields per event, goes

00:00:32.575 --> 00:00:35.178
to a decision model with three yes-or-no questions.

00:00:35.598 --> 00:00:37.320
The three probabilities are averaged.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.451
At zero point six or above, the run becomes a review candidate.

00:00:41.872 --> 00:00:44.004
A person approves or rejects each candidate.

00:00:44.004 --> 00:00:46.441
Nothing in the loop approves on its own.

00:00:46.861 --> 00:00:50.993
Approved runs become skill files that future agents load, and their sessions

00:00:50.993 --> 00:00:52.714
are captured and scored again.

00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:55.758
The whole gate is one line.

00:00:56.358 --> 00:00:58.427
Success: did the run complete its task?

00:00:59.405 --> 00:01:01.716
Reuse: is there a correction worth passing on?

00:01:02.452 --> 00:01:04.672
Evidence: do the trace's events back it up?

00:01:06.082 --> 00:01:09.582
It's a plain average against a fixed constant, so no single answer

00:01:09.582 --> 00:01:10.748
can veto a run.

00:01:12.108 --> 00:01:15.302
The model is asked whether the task succeeded, and whether the

00:01:15.302 --> 00:01:16.464
run holds a correction.

00:01:16.884 --> 00:01:20.940
But every event records exit codes, actors and approvals exactly, and

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.414
the projection drops them.

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:25.364
Only the reuse question really needs a model.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.267
Let the record answer what it knows exactly; spend the model only

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.017
on what a regex can't: is this lesson reusable?

00:01:35.275 --> 00:01:39.318
To recap: capture everything, grade finished runs after the loop, and let

00:01:39.318 --> 00:01:41.676
a person decide what becomes a skill.

00:01:42.096 --> 00:01:44.102
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:44.102 --> 00:01:44.675
I'm Birch.

00:01:44.675 --> 00:01:44.961
Bye!
